# Aether Interface Architecture (.clinerules)

## 0. Strict Git & Repository Invariant (ZERO TOLERANCE)
- NEVER run any `git` commands under any circumstances.
- All version control (`git add`, `commit`, `push`, `checkout`, `reset`, etc.) is strictly reserved for the human developer.
- Focus strictly on editing files, inspecting code, and running explicitly authorized test commands.

## 1. Operating Rules & Pre-Flight Check
- Surgical, minimal diffs only. Zero unsolicited refactoring.
- Check `docs/SYSTEM_MAP.md` before altering cross-module boundaries or adding files.
- If a task introduces a module or shifts an IPC boundary, update `docs/SYSTEM_MAP.md` as the final step.
- Zero zombie code: delete replaced or superseded stubs immediately.

## 2. Dynamic Geometry & Layout
- Zero hardcoded pixel fallbacks or magic tier dimensions in QML. Query layout coordinates dynamically.
- Single-Stroke Rule: Slate cards must have exactly one root visual element with `border.width > 0`.

## 3. Typographic Identity & AI Voice
- AI dialogue across all surfaces binds strictly to `Theme.fontAiVoice` (`Cabinet Grotesk` Regular static cut).
- Dialogue color must use `Theme.aiVoiceGlacial` (`#BAE6FD` / Sky-200) at 1.45 line height.
- All prompts and living context assemble exclusively via `AetherContextBuilder`.

## 4. Concurrency & Telemetry
- GUI thread never invokes background `QThread` workers directly—use PyQt signals/slots.
- Telemetry ring buffers must use fixed-capacity `collections.deque(maxlen=120)` with numeric scalars only.
- Pass raw engine states verbatim (`LATENT`, `WORKING`, `DISTILLING`, `OFFLINE`). Never swallow into boolean gates.
- Database connections must enforce WAL mode, incremental auto-vacuum, and `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;`.

## 5. Test Diet (Rule 10)
- Do NOT create new test files or cases for refactors, visual polish, or tweaks.
- Zero wall-clock sleeps: never use `time.sleep()` or hardcoded `QTest.qWait(ms)`. Use deterministic condition polling (`qtbot.waitUntil`).
- Authorized test runs only. Report exact files modified, test assertions verified, and manual visual verification steps.
